^CONVERSION ERROR$
unexpected expression: struct_tag
found no match for symbol 'swap'
\* identifier: std::tag-__not_<
--
End-to-end `goto-cc` regression for the SFINAE-leak fix landed
alongside cbmc-cpp/cpp11_std_is_swappable_sfinae.

User-reported bug (prior to fix): running
  goto-cc harness.cpp
on source that `#include <array>`s `std::array<double, N>` emitted
spurious type-checker errors
  error: unexpected expression: struct_tag
  error: found no match for symbol 'swap'
with an `irep::pretty()` dump leaked into the error text, and
failed to produce a goto binary despite exit code 0.

Fixed by wrapping per-candidate function-template substitution
and default TYPE template argument substitution with a
null-message-handler per [temp.deduct]/7-8, so SFINAE failures no
longer leak diagnostics.

`std::array<double, 3> a{}` now compiles cleanly through the
goto-cc + cbmc chain.
